│ patch_description        │ This version switches from long-horizon indicator stacking to a regime-robust,            │
│                          │ short-memory feature design. Instead of relying on absolute levels from 20–60 bar         │
│                          │ windows, it emphasizes rolling z-scores, short lookbacks, and rate-of-change features     │
│                          │ that are more stable across market regimes. It also adds a few compact interaction terms  │
│                          │ such as momentum × volatility regime, and uses a more conservative XGBoost configuration  │
│                          │ to reduce overfitting while preserving enough expressivity to avoid prediction collapse.  │
│                          │ The goal is to improve validation slope and predicted dispersion by making features more  │
│                          │ stationary and less dependent on the training regime.                                     │
